cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use labelrank, please cite it as below."
title: "labelrank: ranking a trait-labelled branch-selection test among same-shaped labels on the same tree"
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
abstract: >-
  labelrank calibrates a trait-labelled branch-selection test (HyPhy RELAX or PAML codeml branch-site model A)
  against every other label of the same shape on the same tree. It writes one run per label and seed, runs them
  with the same command, takes each model at its best log-likelihood over seeds, and reports the observed label's
  rank over all alternatives and over the length-matched ones, with optional sequential stopping (Besag and
  Clifford 1991) and batch use over many genes.
keywords:
  - molecular evolution
  - relaxed selection
  - RELAX
  - branch-site test
  - codeml
  - phylogenetics
  - calibration
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: MinSeo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7085-5573"
    affiliation: "Department of Applied Biosciences, Kyungpook National University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sunsungkim04-sys/labelrank"
license: MIT
